[{:seon.task/name "a-view-of-a-pulled-entity-records-its-datom-keys"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: web's successor (filed by context 2026-11-14, root's ruling). Today a component's reads of the pulled tree (seon.ctx's :tree, read through seon.ratom views) are tracked by path (seon.ratom/read-index, reached; the walk's :tree-readers) and matched against the tree's diff (seon.ctx/changes), beside the datom keys its store reads record (the walk's :readers). Hypothesis [H]: one key shape suffices: a view over a pulled entity that carries :db/id records [:ea e a] for a read of attribute a, and an iteration of a join records the key of the join's ref attribute, which the pull pattern gives (a forward ref [:ea e ref], a reverse one [:av ref e]); the tree's non-datom parts (environment keys, root's :process and :health, windows by position) stay ratom values under the path index. Decided by a red proof first: a component that read one attribute of a pulled entity reruns on a commit of that attribute and not on a sibling's, matched by datom keys alone, with the cost proof seon.render-cost-test/a-request-made-again-costs-what-moved unmoved. If it holds, the path index's use for entity reads and seon.ctx/changes as a change signal for them go in the same landing; needs deps' pull precision (datahike.pull-api/a-pull-of-an-attribute-records-its-slice)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"datahike.pull-api/a-pull-of-an-attribute-records-its-slice"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/a-view-of-a-pulled-entity-is-matched-by-its-datom-keys}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-reaction-queue-is-its-owners"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by runtime's Flow survey (notes runtime-flow-survey-2026-11-14.md, H6) [M]: seon.ratom's rea-queue (src/seon/ratom.clj, the reactions a change dirtied, run by flush!) is a process-global defonce volatile, shared by every owner of reactions in the process, as the track cache was until f111c14806. Fix as that was: the queue is its owner's (bound by the owner, as *tracks* is), so two owners' flushes never run each other's reactions. Proof: two owners each with a dirty reaction, one flush! runs only its own."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ratom-test/a-flush-runs-only-its-owners-reactions}}
]
